**FOR TIM**

1. **Why PIT is slow:** each time a pit goes in, right after you place the cover text, CE re-checks every pipe in the drawing to see which pit sits at each end. For each pipe it looks through the whole drawing six times. CE's own timer in your log says this takes about 0.06 s per pipe. That is about **3 seconds per pit** on a 50-pipe drawing like yours this morning.
2. **On bigger jobs it gets much worse:** with 150 pipes I estimate 30 to 40 seconds per pit. That figure is worked out from the timing above; nobody has measured it.
3. **Why the downpipe fix doesn't help:** the DP speed-up (B-004, in tonight's 3.0.86 install) only switches on while a downpipe is being placed. PIT's pipe re-check doesn't use it.
4. **Second cause:** the first PIT after a drawing's pit and pipe list goes missing spends **10 seconds** rebuilding it before the "Specify pit insertion point" prompt. Your log shows this at 10:00 this morning. It only happens once per drawing.
5. **Third cause:** DP and the other sources run the same full pipe re-check after placing. So DP may still have about 3 seconds left over after B-004.
6. **These parts are not slow:** opening the New Pit window (1 to 2 seconds on your drawing), the label, the cover text and the Pit Schedule refresh.
7. **The robot's "50 to 60 seconds per pit" is mostly the robot waiting.** Your own pits took 16 to 17 seconds each, including your clicks. About 4 to 5 seconds of that was CE working.
8. **My mistake:** at first I counted a 28-second robot gap as CE time. Your own runs showed it was mostly robot. I corrected it before writing; it cost about 10 minutes and no test runs.
9. **Recommended fix (planned only, not built):** give the pipe re-check the same "look at each object once" approach as B-004. It sits behind a new switch, ON by default. The pits each pipe joins come out the same; only the time drops. I expect about 3 seconds to fall under 1, but that is a guess until the robot measures it.

